## [01:05 KST] AMINA Q2 2026 Crypto Review: liquidity migration and ETF outflows
- **URL**: https://aminagroup.com/research/crypto-market-q2-2026-review-liquidity-migration-and-etf-outflows/
- **Source Type**: research
- **Domain**: crypto-structure, macro-liquidity, reflexivity
- **Trading Relevance**: 9
- **Time Horizon**: swing
- **Actionability**: monitor
- **Henry Risk Link**: liquidity, narrative, correlation
- **Why it matters**: AMINA는 Q2 crypto drawdown을 단순 risk-off가 아니라 liquidity migration으로 해석한다. ETF flow, basis trade, stablecoin borrowing, digital asset treasury demand, DeFi collateral confidence가 동시에 약해졌다.
- **Raw excerpt / abstract**: Q2 2026 is best understood as a quarter of liquidity migration rather than a simple drawdown. Six liquidity channels weakened: basis trade stopped paying enough to fund stablecoin borrowing; spot Bitcoin ETF flows turned from support into supply; digital asset treasury demand lost momentum. Spot Bitcoin ETF net flows were about $4.89 billion of net outflows.
- **Cold read**: BTC는 narrative asset이지만 marginal buyer plumbing이 끊기면 narrative만으로 회복하지 않는다. leverage가 줄었어도 stablecoin supply와 basis economics가 회복되지 않으면 rebound는 얇다.
- **Trading insight**: MSTU/MSTR/BTC 관련 exposure는 BTC price보다 ETF flow와 carry economics를 함께 봐야 한다. BTC 하락이 deleveraging 완료처럼 보여도 marginal buyer가 돌아오지 않으면 추격 매수 기대값은 낮다.
- **Change sensor**: Spot BTC ETF net flow, stablecoin supply, perp funding, CME basis, DAT issuance
- **Follow-up question**: BTC bounce가 진짜 demand 회복인지 short covering인지 어떻게 구분할 것인가?

