- **Actionability**: monitor
- **Henry Risk Link**: liquidity, execution, narrative
- **Why it matters**: BTC ETF는 단순한 demand wrapper가 아니라 spot market의 시간대별 liquidity 구조를 바꾼다. ETF NAV benchmark fixing window 때문에 3 pm to 4 pm New York time spot volume이 집중되고, US-regulated exchanges의 중요도가 커진다. MSTU/MSTR/BTC 관련 exposure를 볼 때 weekend crypto pattern과 weekday ETF plumbing을 구분해야 한다.
- **Raw excerpt / abstract**: Kaiko states BTC ETF approval led to increased volumes around US market hours, trading uptick toward the end of US trading during benchmark fixing windows, and improved liquidity on benchmark constituent exchanges. Reference rates use trade data between 3 pm and 4 pm New York time. The fixing window accounted for over 6.7% of all volume in Q1, up from 4.5% in Q4 2023; weekday US market close accounts for over 6.6% of benchmark-exchange volume while weekends drop to just over 4%.
- **Cold read**: ETF adoption institutionalizes BTC time. Crypto가 24/7 시장이어도 marginal liquidity는 TradFi clock에 더 묶인다.
- **Trading insight**: BTC breakout이나 reversal을 해석할 때 시간대와 ETF fixing flow를 분리해야 한다. Henry가 BTC-linked exposure를 거래한다면 weekend thin liquidity와 weekday fixing-window volume concentration을 다르게 취급해야 한다.
- **Change sensor**: BTC benchmark fixing volume share, Coinbase close-hour volume, weekend volume share, ETF creation-redemption activity
- **Follow-up question**: BTC signal의 신뢰도는 NY close fixing window 전후에 어떻게 달라지는가?

