- **Raw excerpt / abstract**: ASHRAE says grid-interactive design uses real-time communication with the local or regional grid to optimize energy consumption and provide fast load response, reserve capacity, energy export, and other flexibility. AI training can have large millisecond-level load variations that jeopardize grid stability. It highlights demand response, on-site and off-site renewables, storage, microgrids, emissions-aware computing, OpenADR, IEEE 1547, IEEE 2030.5, FERC Order 2222, and dynamic incentives. It notes energy price alone may not move hyperscalers because energy is a small fraction of total data center operating cost.
