- **Raw excerpt / abstract**: The note finds that over 2017-2019 QT, repo rate sensitivity to issuance increased as the Fed balance sheet shrank. In the current QT period, sensitivity has mostly been small and statistically insignificant but has increased over the past six months. Recent estimates imply a $100 billion increase in Treasury coupon issuance raised the TGCR minus ON RRP spread by approximately 5-6 basis points. Higher reserves and ON RRP take-up mute issuance effects.
